{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-39128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $y=4-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis for $-2\\le x\\le 2.$ Given that the area of the plate is $\\frac{32}{3},$ find the $y$-coordinate of its centroid." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-39128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area ${A}_{D}$ is given by $({x}_{c},{y}_{c}),$ where\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}x\\,\\,\\text{d}A,\\,{y}_{c}=\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/assets/536f542f535513430311b29f43f6fbafb37832d6dfde3b9c81e82237cb011821.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand ${A}_{D}=\\frac{32}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-coordinate of the centroid is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{c} & =\\frac{1}{{A}_{D}}{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{32}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{32}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=4-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{64}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(16-8{x}^{2}+{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{64}{[16x-\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{64}[(32-\\frac{64}{3}+\\frac{32}{5})-(-32+\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{32}{5})] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-39128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40ee775acd8d1020ab4015f9ddb04c169e7b64a57ac0a12629e6c0670bd6322c"} {"question" "q-39128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-39128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-39128" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The lamina $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$ Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and $\\lambda (x,y)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡y[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot {[{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}3{sin}^{2}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{sin}^{3}⁡y]}_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163061" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40ee775acd8d1020ab4015f9ddb04c169e7b64a57ac0a12629e6c0670bd6322c"} {"question" "q-163061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163061" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the lamina that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}$ and has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=y.$ Given that the mass of the lamina is $\\frac{9}{4}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x(\\frac{x}{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{9}{2})}{(\\frac{9}{4})}=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163165" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40ee775acd8d1020ab4015f9ddb04c169e7b64a57ac0a12629e6c0670bd6322c"} {"question" "q-163165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163165" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)={x}^{3}$ and is enclosed between the curve $y=x$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 2.$ Given that the mass of the plate is $\\frac{32}{5}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $m={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/assets/a042919f73d668cac20ead2752c689e57880f60bc096747f41cec3aeb3ed62ca.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le x}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)={x}^{3}.$ \n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}y{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{12}{x}^{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{16}{3})}{(\\frac{32}{5})}=\\frac{5}{6}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163280" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40ee775acd8d1020ab4015f9ddb04c169e7b64a57ac0a12629e6c0670bd6322c"} {"question" "q-163280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{16}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163280" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}$ is enclosed between the line $x=y$ and the line $x=1$ for $1\\le y\\le 2.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type II plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/assets/6cfa58d15b2a1f05aa4d4d088d44b44d6b3225084f627bc8078617d85d801957.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le y,\\,1\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot \\frac{y}{x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{y}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[{\\int }_{1}^{y}\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[x]_{x=1}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y(y-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}-y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-2)-(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40ee775acd8d1020ab4015f9ddb04c169e7b64a57ac0a12629e6c0670bd6322c"} {"question" "q-163584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"} {"question" "q-163584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073832/state.json" "file_sha256" "c0c56e83afaf12d2e798f555d4739b792bf9f67750984d303653a6e77c36008d"}] "usage" {"q-163061" [] "q-39128" []} "basis" 2708 "retractions"